### ZR/ZF scope correction

The independently audited ZR/ZF theorem is a theorem about the **nonisolated positive-contact core** `V`, not the full source. With `v=|V|`,

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3,
\]

and therefore

\[
e+h\ge2v-2,
\qquad
h\ge\delta\ge\lceil D\rceil.
\]

Contact-isolated source points remain in the global configuration. Extending the core stress matrix by zero rows and columns creates additional kernel directions. `C-ZRF-FULL-SOURCE` remains rejected. No bound on the isolated source population follows from ZR/ZF.

### Current C-II frontier

Audit.59 controls theorem authority.

All audit.52--58 results remain canonical. Audit.59 adds the adaptive strict-safe saturation theorem.

For any finite deletion set \(R\) and any bounded measurable
\[
S\subset\operatorname{int}K
\]
strictly farther than one from every retained source point,
\[
E_C(R)=\varnothing
\Longrightarrow
\operatorname{area}S\le\frac{\sqrt3}{2}|R|,
\]
while
\[
E_C(R)\ne\varnothing
\Longrightarrow
\operatorname{area}S\le\frac{\sqrt3}{2}(|R|-1).
\]

In particular, after deleting one contact-active vertex, the entire old hull interior is still covered by unit disks centered at the remaining source points.

This rules out strict-safe **area averaging** as a way to obtain net refill credit after contact breaking. Deleting wall guards and recovering collar area cannot, by itself, force enough points of a lattice with spacing \(>1\) to repay the deletions.

### Exact remaining split

1. **Full-core branch.** Audit.58 supplies finite fan/packet motions that localize all surviving failures to lower blockers or uncovered anchors. Audit.59 says their repair cannot come merely from recovered strict-safe mean area after deleting contact-active points. A closing theorem must use an explicit discrete packet, exact unit-contact packing, collective contact recreation, a non-repacking finite motion, or an exact unit triangle.

2. **Macroscopic-container branch.** The same no-go applies: mean strict-safe area cannot fund the diameter cover. Audit.54 refill remains valid once actual discrete packing capacity is certified.

The short-wall zero-capacity theorem and fixed-wall lock regressions remain binding.

